# Act 1

\\ note: ~Important notes: Side images automatically hide when their characters dialogue is not on screen.~
\\ ~ act 1 · standard deviation ~
\\ scene: classroom_afternoon
\\ music: school_casual
\\ nvl
The warm afternoon light spread itself through the classroom.
The small squeaks from a whiteboard marker softly filled the air.
Pages turns and pens quitely drag across the pages one after the other.
On the far end of the classroom, one student eyes remains fixed on the window.
\\ cg: cg01_act01_lelouch_window_1
His head held softly in his hand as he waits for the seconds to pass by.
The glass softly relayed his shape to him as he drifted. He watches how the light
refracts around his reflection, the edges of his shape softening as the light slowly
drifts in and out the room.
\\ adv
te "Lelouch."
The boy eye remains fixed on the window a second longer before turning slightly
towards the front of the class.
\\ cg: cg01_act01_lelouch_window_2
lelouch:: school_bored center
l "Yes?"
They make eye contact for half a second before the boy looks away again.
te "Can you answer the question?"
His eyes drifts lazily to the board where a function and a graph waited for him.
"Find the inflection point for } y = x^3 - 3x^2 + 2"
lelouch:: school_bored_ec center
\\ note: ~ec : eyes closed, default: eyes open.~
l "x equals one.."
\\ note: ~side sprites will only show when character dialogue is called.~
His eyes linger on the board for a second longer before returning to the window,
his reflection now refraced in a slightly different way.
t "Correct!"
t "As expected."

Lelouchʼs eyes slightly narrow at the sentiment.
As expected...
\\ cg: cg01_act01_lelouch_window_1
\\ nvl
His teachers lectures slowly dissolves into the hums of everyday life. The little
unique gradients of the window seems much more interesting.
There was a standard rythmn to each and every part of Lelouchʼs life.


The bell rings, sit down, listen, answer leave.
Even the abstract concept of the everday can be broken down into defined,
repetitive segments.
Wake up, Brush your teeth, go school go home and rest.
Itʼs something Lelouch knows all to well.
It wasnʼt nessacarily exhausting, for it to be exhausting implies theres active
resistance.
It was more like every aspect of his life was set in stone, pre determined like a tile
in a geomatric pattern.
Routine, as one might say.
A nessacary evil if you crave stability and order in your life.
But, to him it just felt like his life moved forward in a perfect line.
One without deviation, one without purpose, one without resolve.
He vaguely wonders if a life like his was ideal, a calm peaceful life without
interruption.
But what is a line without direction?
He slightly smirks to himself as the absurdity of the line, rolling his fingers one
after each other on the surface of his desk as if it would make time pass any faster.

The bells soft chime came shortly after, slowly the air fills with the minor babble of
his classmates as they begin to pack up for the day.
However the day was not over yet.
\\ hide: cg

Lelouch quietly rises from his seat, placing his maths book into his bag without
much thought, before making his way to the door.
\\ scene: school_hallway

Soft pats fluttered as Lelouch makes his way down the hall.
He stands there for a moment in front of the student council room, his hand
applying light pressure to the door handle.
As if he is preparing himself for the meeting.
He opens it, and steps inside.
\\ scene: student_council_room
\\ music: school_fun
\\ adv
rivalz:: school_stressed center
r "Oh come on! Imagine the publicity!"
r "Local school pulls off pizza world record."
r "I can just hear the money rolling in."
rivalz:: school_stressed right t_slideright
nina:: school_sigh center
n "Rivalz, that is structural absurd."
\\ hide: rivalz
rivalz:: school_passionate right
r "It is if you donʼt believe!"
r "Come on, lelouch-back me up!"
\\ note: ~lelouch side image will show instead of sprite. side image and sprites same image just different location / cropping.~
lelouch:: school_baffled center
l "...Huh?"
rivalz:: school_passionate right t_shake
The state of the room immediately sticks out to him.
Papers were spread absentmindely across the desk, Rivalz clutches a good
number of pages to his chest as he tries so vigilantly to defend his idea.
His gaze moves across the room.
Rivalz, loud and defensive
Nina, tense in pure disbelief.
Shirley, hands clasp together, clearly fond of rivalz idea.
And Milly, laid back in her chair, arms cross , loving the chaos stiring in the room.
\\ clear
Lelouch sets his bag down and moves to sit in his usual seat, scratching the back
of his head amongst the absurdity, more out of habit than thought.
lelouch:: school_bored center
l "You want my honest opinion?"

rivalz:: school_starstruck right
r "Obviously!"
l "..."
lelouch:: school_bored_ec center
l "Itʼs impratical."
milly:: school_teasing_ec center
m "Unfortunate. :P"
\\ hide: rivalz
rivalz:: school_stressed right t_shake
r "Thatʼs not helpful!"
lelouch:: school_smirk center
l "You didnt ask for helpful.."
\\ hide: rivalz
rivalz:: school_passionate right t_shake
r "Come on man-Imagine it!"
r "How hard can a giant pizza be?!"
r "Milly clearly got the funds for it."

milly:: school_sigh center
m "and how am I going to explain that we spent seventy-five percent of the fesitvals budget"
m "on a 62 inch pizza."
lelouch:: school_baffled center
l ".. 62 inches?"
Lelouch reaches forward to lift one of pages has tumbled out of rivalzʼs tight
embrace, and skims over it.
r "The budget resets next term—"
r "And besides, we only have a few months left."
r "Letʼs do something people will actually remember!"
shirley:: school_happy left
sh "I think thatʼs a wonderful idea Rivalz!"
\\ hide: shirley
shirley:: school_sweatdrop right
sh "Though... Iʼm not sure we have an oven that can fit a pizza that... wide."
lelouch:: school_think center
l "...It could work"
\\ hide: rivalz
rivalz:: school_starstruck right t_shake
r "See?! Lelouchʼs on my side-now we have to do it!"
\\ hide: milly
milly:: school_think center
m "hmm? Didnʼt you just say it was impratical?"
lelouch:: school_bored center
l "I mean... it is."
lelouch:: school_smirk center
l "But impratical doesnʼt exactly mean impossible."
l "I see the potential."
Lelouch sets the loose page back down and glances at the clock for a second.
r "Well? are you waiting for? Lay it on us!"
lelouch:: school_think center
l "Instead of one large pizza..."
l "Couldnʼt we just divide it into multiple slices and arrange it as one large one?"
lelouch:: school_explain center
l "That way, weʼd achieve the same effect"
l "With the limits we actually have."
l "While retaining the memorable aspect."
The council pauses for a second.
\\ hide: rivalz
rivalz:: school_think right
r "Wait.."
rivalz:: school_passionate right t_shake
r "That actually sounds doable-"


r "Lelouch you genius!"
\\ hide: shirley
nina:: school_think left
n "It would certaintly maintain itʼs structural intergrity.."
r "And look really flipping cool!!!"
\\ hide: milly
milly:: school_think center
m "hmm.."
m "now that I can approve off."
\\ hide: milly
milly:: school_tease center
m "As long as we dont set any ovens on fire."

lelouch:: school_polite center
l "Just a thought."
\\ clear
\\ nvl
Lelouch returns to watching the clock tick. The second hand ticks forward while
the first remains stagnant on the hour.
For a moment the chaos within the student council room dwindles, a small
suggestion causing ideals to align.
It all makes sense, but lelouch canʼt help but feel detatch from it all.
Rivalz immediately jumps back to his seat, hastily pushing all his loose papers
towards him so he can revise his grand plan, the others going back to pitching
their own ideas for the school festival.

A chair softly shifts towards lelouch, Shirley leaning closer, just enough that only
lelouch can hear her.
\\ adv
shirley:: school_warm center
sh "I didnʼt see you in the common room last period,"
sh "Did you just come from maths?"
Lelouch turns to face her with a mild expression,
lelouch:: school_bored center
l "Yeah, something like that."
\\ hide: shirley
shirley:: school_giggle center
Shirley lets out a small laugh, flashing him her signature warm smile.
sh "Well, Iʼm glad you could make it today,"
sh "Things were getting a little heated before you arrived.."
lelouch:: school_polite center
Lelouch subtly smiles back, just enough to keep her satisfied.
l "Just playing my part.."
\\ hide: shirley
shirley:: school_default center
sh "Oh-Right!"


sh "Suzaku isnʼt in again is he?"
\\ hide: shirley
shirley:: school_sad center
sh "Thatʼs the second time this week.."
".."
lelouch:: school_default center
l "He mentioned something about family matters."
sh "Oh really?"
sh "I hope heʼs okay.."
Lelouch nods lightly,
lelouch:: school_polite center
l "Yeah, Iʼm sure itʼs nothing serious"
sh "Yeah!"
sh "And hopefully you can get him up to speed!"
sh "Heʼd love the giant pizza.."
lelouch:: school_polite center
l "Of course.."
Her smile lingers for a moment longer before rivalz steals her attention away for
approval on his pizza measurements.
\\ clear
His smile fades, his gaze returning to the clock again, waiting
patiently for the day to end.
\\ nvl

His fellow council members voices shifted to those of farewells as the day finally
came to an end.
He retrieves his bag and trades brief goodbyes before making his way towards the
school gates.
\\ music: autumn_calm
Once outside, he clicks his phone on, intending on checking the time. Only to be
met with a small reminder he set on his phone a day prior.
\\ adv
lelouch:: school_default center
l "Right, the cakes. Nunnallyʼs preparing tea today isnʼt she."
\\ nvl
He returns his phone back to his coat pocket, before making a u turn towards the
small shopping district close to the school.
The idle conversation of his fellow students pass by him as he walks amongst
them.
A particularly loud group of boys walk past him, eating cheap takoyaki while
arguing about an anime lelouch couldnʼt quite catch.


On the other side, a couple sits close together, sharing a comfortable silence as
the breeze moves between them.
Lelouch briefly watches, then looks ahead.

it all felt so mundane.
He considers it for a moment, so is he.
Lelouch walks the same route he always took to the district, down to the same
path. He knows exactly how long it takes, 10 minutes to and back.
He knows it without thinking, just like everything else.
What makes this any different from anyone else?
He shrugs off the thoughts, there were much more pressing matters he needs to
focus on.
Nunnally is patiently waiting at home for him, usually this time the tea is already set.
2 cups of green tea she was insisted would fair nicely with a slice of strawberry
shortcake if the price wasnʼt too high.
Lelouch had obviously agreed, not one to frequently say no to his little sister,
especially to unnessaracry purchases he knew would make her day.
They werent exactly well off, their home was small and quaint compared to the
grand estates of some of his classmates.
The school covers most of it, thanks to Milly.
Itʼs convenient.
Tea time used to be something they all shared, his mother setting down the plates
and pouring the tea instead of Nunnally.
Small loving conversations about school and their day around the dinner table.
Unfortunately, small routines tend to die as quickly as their picked up..
His father on the otherhand is... elsewhere.
Lelouch exhaled quietly, his hands snug within his coat pockets as he continued
down the tree lined street.
Nothing about his life is exactly difficult. Repetitive yes, but managable.


He has food, he has a roof over him and his sisterʼs head and he has enough to
provide for her with the small money he has.
And when things are out of his reach, the school does.
Stable, predictable, and yet he canʼt seem to shake off the feeling that heʼs
waiting.
For something, anything. A reason, a direction.
Something that isnʼt already decided.
However, Nunnally smiles each time he comes home, that matters. Even if she
couldnʼt see him fully.
And, if anything ever happened, Suzaku would always be there. Ready to help,
ready to protect.
Lelouchʼs eyes narrow softly at the thought for a moment, before shrugging the
feeling off.
Lelouch eventually reached the end of the path, to the point where it splits.
Right - the quick way to the shops.
Left - the longer route through the woods.

Heʼs taken the right path every time.
Today, without really deciding, he turns left.
\\ scene: forest_clearing
\\ music: forest_theme
The hustle and bustle of his fellow students gradually begins to drown out behind
him. Though he was never that close to begin with.
The maple trees that once lined the street grow denser, the narrow pavement
cutting off abruptly.
The pavement was now replaced by a rugged dirt path.
He keeps walking.
The air cools around him, it feels heavier as if the breeze was pressing down on
his skin.
A gust of wind passes by..


The inside of the forest was a sight to behold in of itself.
Strong rays of light filters through the maple canopy, bouncing off the deep red
leaves to leave little fragments of red and gold on the forest floor.
His steps slow down without him meaning to.
The usual numbness within his chest remains, but now something else restlessly
stirs beneath it.
A faint awareness.
The little grumbles of gravel rubbing on dirt filled the air as he continues to make
his way through..
A single leaf spirals down in front of him, landing on the dirt path with an unatural
softness.
then—
\\ sfx: rustle
Rustle.
His eyes dart to the thicker underbush on his right, nothing moved.
He keeps walking.
The trees crowd closer together, the golden fragments of light grow few and far
between, a deep shadow manifesting in their place.
\\ sfx: rustle_closer
Rustle.
Closer this time..
Another sound growled through the air, a croak that a few leaves couldnʼt have
possibly made.
Itʼs long and uneven, dragging through the air.
Lelouch stops in his tracks, his feet now planted firmly on the gravel as he looks
around.
His fingers tighten softly inside his pockets.
His gaze sharpens, albeit slightly, but enough.
\\ adv
lelouch:: school_startled center
l "..."
l "...Hello?"
The sound stops.


A small, needy breath takes its place.
one frail, not his.
"...p-"
The sound breaks..
"...please..."
Heʼs still..
The plea lingers in the air, it felt too directed to be an animal, but too raw for it to be
a person.
"...blood."
The air grows heavier by the second, the pleas gradually growing in volume.
and desperation.
Lelouch steps forward.
The calls grow clear with each step he took.
The wetness of its voice.
The heavy strain in its vocal chords.
The tremors that lingered in each call it draws out.
It pulled him forward.
The thick maple trees thin slightly.
And then he stops.
\\ cg: cg02_act01_forest
A dark liquid pools at his feet, a dark maroon staining the ground and everything
near it.
Itʼs spread across the ground thick and uneven, some parts dried across the white
bell flowers that sat beside it.
lelouch:: school_shocked center
l "...Blood..?"
His gaze drifts upwards.
A lithe figure lies at the centre of it all, deathly still.

\\ nvl
A girl, close to his age. Her clover hair fanned outward amongst the blood, her
strands clinging together in grotesque clumps where the liquid has soaked
through.

Her eyes are open, a dimmed gold that were glazed over. Her pupils blown and
unfocused.
She remains still.
Lelouchʼs eyes continue to drift, much to his dismay.
They latch on to her chest.
A stake, driven clean but forcefully through her chest.
The wood tinted a sickly red in all the places it had the most contact with her
blood.
His feet remain planted on the grass, the sticky substance slowly making contact
with his shoes as it spread.
His hands begin to tremble at the obscene sight, a knot in his throat forming.
\\ adv
"....blood..."
"...p-please.."
Her eyes shift slowly, landing on him..
lelouch:: school_shocked center
l "...What?"
"...bloood.."
"...pelase..."
l "..."
l "..why..?"
lelouch:: school_shocked center
l "What are you—"
"...please.."
Softer words now, more desperate than anything sheʼs said prior.
Lelouch doesnʼt move, he cannot bring himself to.
His eyes drop down to the blood for a moment then back to her.

\\ nvl
and then, something in his head clicks.
He moves, his legs thinking before he could.
He kneels beside her carefully, her blood now staining his knees through his
school uniform.
Gently, his hands wander to the underside of her shoulders. Sheʼs warm,
incredibly warm.
He lifts her, pulling her into a mock embrace so that her weight settled against
him, sheʼs incredibly light.
for a second, the world lingers for a moment.
And then she moves.
\\ cg: cg03_act01_feed
Two sharp points pierce his neck. The pain was bright and clean.
A sharp hiss mixed with a groan escapes his lips as his neck swells with pain for a
brief agonizing second.
It flares for a moment then immediately dissolves into something else.

Into a strange sickly warmth.
As a deep, rhythmic suction begins.
The warmth first concentrates in his neck, before slowly crawling through his
body, through his chest down to his arms and into the very finger tips that holds
her in place.
His grip around her instinctively tightens, each suck feels like a gentle tug as she
slowly pulls more and more blood out of him.
The more she drank, the more he felt something deep in his soul pulling at him.
His thoughts began to blur together in a frenzy, slowly falling into a state of
intoxicating euphoria mixed with genuine light headedness from the blood loss.
The crisp sharp edges of the maple leaves begins to warp, slowly dissolving into a
visual symphony of red green and yellow.
The loving song of a robin dulled into a buzz.
In their place, something else settles in, one that is heavy, quiet but certain.


For a moment, he isnʼt empty.
Each pull hollows him out further, and yet it feels filling.
He felt... Seen.
Needed.
The explicit details of his feelings begin to blur along with the fabric of his reality.
His fragile body slowly untangles before laying limp in her arms.
\\ adv
"t—thank you.."
"..."
"..."
"Lelouch?"
"Lelouch!"
\\ break
\\ scene: hospital_room_afternoon
\\ music: lelouch_theme
\\ nvl
The afternoon light, once warm, has taken a harsher form. It spilled in through the
slim opening of the blinds, claiming anything that found itself on its path.
Lelouchʼs eyes being one of the poor victims.
His eyes immediately clenched, not used to the direct sunlight before gradually
opening again. Small beeps permeate the air in even intervals, it sounds rough
around the edges which seemed to amplify Lelouchʼs incoming headache.
His ears weakly graze over to the left, he could hear faint chatter in the
background.
What sounded to be a doctor speaking in a quiet, controlled tone.
\\ adv
"—Is severely anemic."
"But his levels have managed to stabilize unusually fast.."
"Unfortunately, we werenʼt able to locate a source for the blood loss."
"But we are glad to say that a blood transfusion will not be nessacary."
A familiar voice rang out.
"Thatʼs great news. Thank you for all your hard work."
The boy slightly turns back to the bed, their eyes latching on to each other.


Immediately,
2 surprisingly firm arms find themselves wrapped around Lelouchʼs now upright
self.
\\ cg: cg04_act01_hospital
His arms however awkwardly above the boy, before returning the hug.
lelouch:: hospital_confused center
l "Suzaku?"
\\ note: ~dialogue within cgs will have side images for everyone.~
suzaku:: shrine_relieved left
s "Thank god."
He pulls back.
suzaku:: shrine_relieved left
"I thought i lost you.."
\\ note: ~flashback shown with graphics~
Blood. A lot of it, pooling from the center.
The warm breath on his neck, the weight on his chest.
suzaku:: shrine_worried left
s "You really shouldnʼt wander like that Lelouch..."
l "..."
suzaku:: shrine_worried left
s "Lelouch?"
lelouch:: hospital_absentminded center
l "Yeah, Iʼm sorry.."
His fingers find themselves at the back of his neck like always.
They lightly graze over 2 swollen bumps.
lelouch:: hospital_absentminded center
l "..."
Their clean, almost fully healed except for 2 rough scabs that had been easily
spaced out.
They linger there a second longer, a sickly feeling arises within his chest,
drawing him to something, somewhere.
lelouch:: hospital_think center
l "I see.."
d "It seems like youʼve fully awakened, Iʼm glad."
d "I will let the others know."
d "Try not to strain yourself, alright?"
Lelouch returned a weak nod.
The doctor quietly exits the room, leaving the two boys alone.

suzaku:: shrine_worried left
s "..."
s "I found you.."
s "You were just lying there, surrounded by blood."
s "Like a disturbing amount."
s "Iʼm glad the ambulance came as quickly as they did."
lelouch:: hospital_confused center
l "w—What happened?.."
suzaku:: shrine_explain left
s "Well um."
s "I had been out there already.."
s "Strange reports, mainly animals."
s "So i thought iʼd check it out."
Lelouchʼs gaze shifts to the iv bag stationed next to him. A thin line of red drips
downwards.
suzaku:: shrine_worried left
s "You werenʼt even that far in.."
s "Just off the main path.."
s "... It looked like you had just been dropped there."
l "..."
s "And you were cold."
s "Pale, like youʼd been there for hours."
suzaku:: shrine_think left
s "But that doesnʼt make any sense."
s "And i couldnt find where the blood had came from."
lelouch:: hospital_neutral center
l "Strange."
A quiet breath escapes Suzakuʼs lips.
suzaku:: shrine_worried left
s "I tried to wake you."
s "Shook you, called your name."
s "Nothing."
s "You didnʼt react at all."


s "When the ambulance arrived, they said youʼd already been out there for a few hours."
suzaku:: shrine_think left
s "It was just so..."
s "Weird."
s "You scared me you know.."
His hands settled gently on Lelouchʼs shoulder.
suzaku:: shrine_warm left
s "Just.."
s "Dont do that again, alright?"
lelouch:: hospital_polite center
l "..I wont.."
His gaze finds itself back on the iv drip, following the thick lines of blood each drop.
suzaku:: shrine_smile left
s "The doctor said you can be officially discharged tomorrow.."
lelouch:: hospital_confused center
l "...Already?"
suzaku:: shrine_smile left
s "Iʼm going to stay the night at your place tonight.. Nunnallyʼs worried sick."
Suzaku brushes off his uniform and rises.
s "Get some rest okay?"
s "Iʼll see you tomorrow."
\\ hide: suzaku
Suzaku shoots him a quiet small smile, before leaving, quietly sliding the door
behind him.
\\ nvl
The silence in the room resumes, only broken occasionally by the soft chime of
the heart monitor.
\\ adv
"...p—please.."
\\ nvl
Lelouchʼs half lidded eyes widen for a second, his head looking left and right
weakly to find the source of the noise.
Thereʼs no one there.
His hand rises slowly, to the back of his neck.
He doesnʼt pull it away.
\\ break
